Dear CIP friends,

there is a small core group of developers that will be available at ELCE 
to answer (almost) all the questions you might have about the project or 
a specific technology or technical issue... you might have.

This meeting will be also ideal for those who know very little about the 
project and have basic questions. I personally recommend you to attend 
if you are simply interested in how things are going or what kind of 
work is CIP doing.

We have called this meeting CIP Developers Meeting[1]. It is open and no 
pre-registration is needed.

* When: Tuesday October 24th from 13:00 to 14:00 hours
* Where: Liben Room, Mezzanine Leve; al ELCE venue in Prague CZ.
* For whom: everybody interested in talking to CIP developers including 
CIP kernel maintainers.
* Agenda:
** Short description of the technical activities that CIP is currently 
doing and some planned actions (5 to 10 min )
** Q&A (rest of the session)

Please spread the word.

